# Official Fabric Provider Comparison

Comparative architecture analysis between Microsoft's official Terraform provider ([`microsoft/terraform-provider-fabric`](https://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-fabric), `registry.terraform.io/microsoft/fabric`) and this community extension provider (`registry.terraform.io/jambazid/fabricext`).

---

## Executive Summary

| USP Dimension | `microsoft/fabric` (Official) | `jambazid/fabricext` (Community Extension) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Item-Level Sharing (`Warehouse`, `SQLDatabase`, `Lakehouse`)** | Not supported (workspace-wide role assignments only) | Declarative `fabricext_{warehouse,sql_database,lakehouse}_permission` resources for least-privilege non-member access |
| **Drift Detection & Self-Healing Convergence** | Portal item-share changes go untracked; OneLake roles hit [#1044](https://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-fabric/issues/1044) `objectType` drift | Stateful drift detection & graceful convergence: strips portal privilege creep and restores downgraded shares in place, recreates revoked shares, handles `<item>_id` renames with zero replacement, and preserves OneLake `PrincipalType` |
| **Cross-Plane Effective ACL Verification** | None | Built-in read-back verification plus [`fabricext_item_share_gate`](../resources/item_share_gate.md) Admin API (`GET /v1/admin/.../users`) hard-failure sanity lever |
| **OneLake Zero-Trust & Concurrency** | Preview-only; manual `DefaultReader` cleanup; unserialized calls | GA endpoints, automated `DefaultReader` purge (`fabricext_lakehouse_onelake_security`), and per-Lakehouse mutex + `If-Match` ETag RMW |
| **Hermetic Contract & Drift Testing** | Go struct stubs (`fabcore/fake`); live capacity required for acceptance | Sub-10s hermetic `TF_ACC=1` suite against `fabricmock` (`specs/fabric/` Swagger 2.0) + `pbimock` (`specs/powerbi/metadata/` OAS 3.0.3) with automated drift-injection falsifiers |

### Architectural Trade-Off Analysis

| Dimension | Cost | Impact | Risk |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Declarative Item Sharing** | Low | High: Least-privilege non-member access across all engines | Low: Pin provider versions for upstream service stability |
| **Cross-Plane Share Gate** | Low | High: Independent Admin API verification before downstream tasks | Low: Optional lever (`verify_item_shares = false` for non-admins) |
| **OneLake Specialization** | Low | High: Automated zero-trust `DefaultReader` purging | Low: Distinct `fabricext_*` prefix |
| **OneLake Concurrency** | Low | High: Race-safe updates under parallel `for_each` | Low: Identical import ID format |
| **Offline Test Suite** | Low | High: Sub-10s hermetic `TF_ACC=1` acceptance testing | Low: Continuous Swagger sync checks |

