## Scope & Capabilities Comparison

### Platform Breadth vs Specialization

`microsoft/fabric` is the official general-purpose Terraform provider for Microsoft Fabric infrastructure. It manages workspaces, capacities, domains, and first-wave items (Notebooks, Lakehouses, Warehouses, SQL Databases, Data Pipelines), alongside workspace role assignments.

`jambazid/fabricext` is a specialized security companion provider designed specifically to manage direct item-level sharing permissions and Lakehouse OneLake Data Access Roles with strict concurrency safety and stateful drift self-healing.

### Declarative Item Sharing USP

Microsoft Fabric workspace roles (Admin, Member, Contributor, Viewer) grant broad access across every item in a workspace. For enterprise least-privilege architectures, organizations require granular item-level sharing:

1. **Declarative Item Permissions**: `jambazid/fabricext` provides `fabricext_warehouse_permission`, `fabricext_sql_database_permission`, and `fabricext_lakehouse_permission` to grant non-member principals direct access (such as `["Read"]`, `["Read", "ReadData"]`, or `["Read", "ReadData", "Execute"]`) to specific items without workspace membership.
2. **Stateful Drift Self-Healing**: When item permissions are modified out-of-band in the Fabric portal, `fabricext` detects the drift during refresh and converges back to the declared configuration in place.
3. **Cross-Plane Verification**: Through `fabricext_item_share_gate`, the provider queries the official Fabric Admin API (`GET /v1/admin/workspaces/{workspaceId}/items/{itemId}/users`) to verify that granted permissions are active in effective ACLs before downstream operations proceed.

~> **Note:** Item-level permission resources call internal Power BI service endpoints because Microsoft Fabric does not yet offer a v1 REST write API for item sharing. Endpoint behavior may change without notice; pin provider versions and validate upgrades in non-production workspaces first.

### OneLake Roles Comparison

| Aspect | `microsoft/fabric` (`fabric_onelake_data_access_security`) | `jambazid/fabricext` (`fabricext_lakehouse_data_access_role`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Maturity Gate** | Preview-only (`preview = true` required) | GA endpoints by default |
| **DefaultReader Lifecycle** | None (manual portal intervention required) | Automated verification & zero-trust purge (`fabricext_lakehouse_onelake_security`) |
| **Resource Modes** | Single-mode nested blocks | Dual-mode: simple flat or advanced structured |
| **Item Identification** | UUID only (`item_id`) | UUID (`lakehouse_id`) or display name (`lakehouse_name`) |
| **RLS & CLS** | Supported in `decision_rules` | Supported in `decision_rule` blocks (100% parity) |
| **Members & Shortcuts** | Entra members and shortcut items | Entra members and shortcut items (`fabric_item_member`) |
| **Concurrency** | Direct API calls without client-side serialization | Per-Lakehouse mutex + `If-Match` ETag Read-Modify-Write (RMW) retry |
| **Pagination Safety** | Single-role calls; plural data sources may truncate | Client-side `continuationToken` pagination up to 100 pages with cycle detection |
| **Plan-Time Validation** | Schema syntax validation | Rejects `ReadWrite`/`Write` combined with RLS/CLS; role name $\le 128$ chars |
| **Read-Back Drift** | Fails on omitted `objectType` ([#1044](https://github.com/microsoft/terraform-provider-fabric/issues/1044)) | Preserves `PrincipalType` on empty API read-back |
| **Import ID** | `{workspace_id}/{item_id}/{role_name}` | `{workspace_id}/{lakehouse_id}/{role_name}` (100% parity) |

#### OneLake Roles vs Sharing

Fabric item-level sharing and OneLake Data Access Roles address distinct layers:

- **Item-Level Sharing** (Workspace Item Layer): Governs whether a principal can connect to, read metadata from, or execute queries against a Warehouse, SQL Database, or Lakehouse item. Managed via `fabricext_{warehouse,sql_database,lakehouse}_permission`.
- **OneLake Data Access Roles** (Storage Layer): Governs fine-grained access to Parquet tables, folders, rows (RLS), and columns (CLS) in OneLake storage for Lakehouse items. Managed via `fabricext_lakehouse_data_access_role`.

